01.Index 02.Projects 03.About Contact ← All projects Category Project (2026 — AI agent platform) AI test users that run your real flows — and a backend built like infrastructure. Walkthru is a launch check for apps built with AI. Persona agents try your real signup, onboarding and checkout flows inside your own browser, think aloud, and report exactly where they got stuck — with the step, the screenshot and the reason. The browser is the hands; the server is the brain. Everything that can be code is code: only the persona session is an agent, and every rule about where it may act is enforced on the server. Live at trywalkthru.com. A deployed browser-agent platform with a Chrome extension, durable job queue and remote MCP server. Python / FastAPI / LangGraph / LangSmith / PostgreSQL / Supabase (RLS) / MCP / Chrome MV3 / TypeScript Live siteGitHub repo API tests (+90 extension tests) MCP tools, per-key rate limited deterministic scanners HTTP call per agent step (Engineering) Engineering highlights LangGraph decide → act → check loop with interrupt()/Command(resume) — one HTTP call per step, state in a Postgres checkpointer, API stateless and horizontally scalable Code safety gate (_enforce) re-checked every step: hallucinated elements, pay/delete actions and unverified-site writes are replaced or safely stopped Durable Postgres job queue — FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, 15-minute leases, per-kind attempt budgets, exponential backoff with jitter Multi-provider LLM chain (Claude Haiku on Vertex → Groq gpt-oss → Gemini) behind a circuit breaker with strict per-provider timeouts SSRF-safe fetcher: resolve once, block private/metadata/IPv4-in-IPv6 ranges, pin the connection, re-validate every redirect Remote MCP server (streamable HTTP) — 24 tools, SHA-256-hashed keys, Postgres-backed per-key limits LangSmith evals on easy/hard/showcase fixture sites full of traps; findings without real evidence are dropped in code (01) Browser on the user's machine, brain on the server. A Chrome MV3 extension (WXT, TypeScript) snapshots the DOM including open shadow roots, masks PII in-page, runs axe-core and Core Web Vitals, and executes actions. FastAPI and LangGraph decide. No headless Chromium on servers, so hosting stays near zero and logged-in pages work without anyone sharing a password. (02) One HTTP call per agent step. (03) Prompts are never a safety boundary. (04) Fail soft, never fake. (05) The scanner can't be turned into an SSRF. (06) Grounded, measured, regression-tested. (Next project) Agentic planner↗ Let's talk↗ [email] Write a message Résumé ElsewhereGitHub LinkedIn X Hashnode How to reach meFastest way to reach me is email. LinkedIn works too — I check it daily. Hiring for backend, platform or AI engineering? I reply within a day. LocalKolkata, India · 15:25 Open to backend, AI and platform engineering internships and full-time roles — remote or on-site. © 2026 Rohit Maity Theme 02 / 05

